 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $25.8B in FY2025 [1].\nRevenue CAGR was +7.7% over FY2018..FY2025 [2].\nNet income was $6.8B in FY2025 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2025 was +9.8% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2025 was -1.6% [3] [5].\nIn FY2025, net income growth of -1.6% [3] [5] was below revenue growth of +9.8% [1] [4].\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow growth of -5.8% [6] [7] was below net income growth of -1.6% [3] [5].\n\n## Margins\nOperating margin was 32.1% in FY2025 [8].\nOperating margin changed +0.3pp in FY2025 [8] [9].\nNet margin changed -3.1pp in FY2025 [10] [11].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nThe current ratio was 0.60\u00d7 in FY2025 [12], below 1.00\u00d7.\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow of $12.5B [6] was above net income of $6.8B [3].\nLong-term debt was $89.6B in FY2025 [13].\n\n## Red flags\nLong-term debt grew +234.4% from FY2018 to FY2025. Source operands: Long-term debt USD 26,782,000,000 in FY2018 [14]; Long-term debt USD 89,556,000,000 in FY2025 [13].\nCurrent ratio is below 1.0 (0.60\u00d7 in FY2025). Source operands: Current ratio 0.3640x in FY2018 [15]; Current ratio 0.5953x in FY2025 [12].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from +9.8% in FY2025 [1] [4].\nWatch how net income in the next reporting update compares with $6.8B in FY2025 [3].\nWatch how operating margin in the next reporting update compares with 32.1% in FY2025 [8].",
